  "journal": {
    "survey_kit": {
      "title": "Tools for the Unknown",
      "text": "Orin knew something was wrong before we said a word. When Elara showed him her sketch of the markings he put his hammer down: not a natural crack, he said. We put together a survey kit: compass, rope, chalk, torches and a pickaxe I'm told not to use on anything that matters. Then Orin held the compass near the sketch and the needle swung round to the paper while the whole workshop hummed. Orin is with us now, as our adviser, and his workshop is where we'll mend and supply."
    }
  }
